From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MI50 ROCm compatibility project <mi50@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] PyTorch: make ROCm TF32 capability query device-safe

The PyTorch ROCm TF32 query asks for device properties without first checking
availability. That raises on a CPU-only host and makes pre-hardware packaging
checks fail. Return false when no device is present; the existing gfx906
architecture allow-list continues to reject TF32 on MI50.
---
 torch/cuda/__init__.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/torch/cuda/__init__.py b/torch/cuda/__init__.py
--- a/torch/cuda/__init__.py
+++ b/torch/cuda/__init__.py
@@ -230,5 +230,7 @@ def is_tf32_supported() -> bool:
     r"""Return a bool indicating if the current CUDA/ROCm device supports dtype tf32."""
     if torch.version.hip:
+        if not is_available():
+            return False
         prop_name = torch.cuda.get_device_properties().gcnArchName
         archs = ("gfx94", "gfx95")
         for arch in archs:
-- 
